#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:1
msgid "`kernel/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:3
msgid "Guidelines that apply only to code under `kernel/`."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:5
msgid "Keep the Linux Compatibility docs current (`linux-compat-docs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:7
msgid ""
"When a change under `kernel/` changes the supported system calls, flags, "
"arguments, file systems, sockets, boot protocols, or kernel parameters, "
"update the [Linux Compatibility](../../../../kernel/linux-compatibility/) "
"section in the same PR, so the documented coverage keeps matching the code. "
"This includes adding support, removing support, or restricting supported "
"argument combinations."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:13
msgid ""
"For a **system call**: update the matching [Syscall Flag Coverage]"
"(../../../../kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/) page. Update "
"its [SCML](../../../../kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/"
"system-call-matching-language.md) (`.scml`) coverage file only when the "
"supported invocation patterns change, such as when adding a syscall, flag, "
"ioctl command, or socket option."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:18
msgid ""
"For a **kernel parameter**: update the [Kernel Parameters](../../../../"
"kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md) page."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:20
msgid ""
"For supported **file systems**, **sockets**, or **boot protocols**: update "
"the corresponding [File systems](../../../../kernel/linux-compatibility/"
"#file-systems), [Sockets](../../../../kernel/linux-compatibility/#sockets), "
"or [Boot protocols](../../../../kernel/linux-compatibility/#boot-protocols) "
"section."
msgstr ""

#: src/to-contribute/coding-guidelines/for-documentation/path-specific/kernel.md:25
msgid ""
"Do not update the Linux Compatibility pages when a change fixes a Linux "
"compatibility bug without changing Asterinas's claimed coverage of Linux "
"features."
msgstr ""
